PROMETHEUS AVATAR SDK =E2=80=94 Myths Labs =E2=80=94 TEST NOW
GitHub: https://github.com/myths-labs/prometheus-avatar

Freshness: the repository is currently highly active (234 commits
surfaced), but GitHub=E2=80=99s rendered page did not expose a trustworthy
timestamp for the latest commit, so this is classified as newly discovered
rather than falsely claimed as a release in the last hour.

What it does: an MIT-licensed open-source SDK/runtime for embodied
Live2D/3D AI characters. It combines realtime voice, lip sync,
text=E2=86=92emotion=E2=86=92expression/motion, VTuber camera tracking, plu=
ggable LLM/TTS,
an MCP server, and an AgentSkills-compatible companion skill. The MCP
surface exposes create_avatar, set_avatar_state, equip_asset,
generate_asset, update_asset, generate_image_pro, list_marketplace,
get_avatar_status, share_avatar and speak. The companion skill can push
real agent state (thinking/acting/done) to an avatar over plain HTTP.

Why technically interesting: previous finds gave us pieces of Performance
IR or browser rendering. Prometheus packages embodiment itself as an
agent-callable tool surface. That means an autonomous content agent can
create an identity, change state/expression/assets, speak, and expose its
state without custom UI glue. Its SDK separates renderer, TTS, lip-sync and
emotion interfaces, matching our replaceable-renderer architecture.

Inputs =E2=86=92 outputs: agent/LLM state + text/voice + avatar model/asset=
s =E2=86=92
realtime embodied Live2D/3D character with speech, lip-sync, expressions
and motions.

Availability: runnable public code, npm SDK, MCP server, examples,
marketplace/platform and agent skill. MIT for the repository;
bundled/sample Live2D models have their own licenses, so production
identities should use assets with explicit commercial rights.

Latency/hardware: README claims ~200 ms realtime voice latency through
Gemini Live WebSocket. Visual rendering is browser-side Live2D/3D rather
than diffusion video, so it belongs in the cheap/live layer, not the
premium photoreal renderer.

Maturity: RUNNABLE.

Relevance: very high for persistent AI hosts because it turns avatar
embodiment into a stable agent API rather than tying character state to one
renderer.

EXACT EXPERIMENT
Take our Performance IR and map five canonical operations into Prometheus:
SPEAK, STATE, AFFECT, ACTION and EQUIP. Run one AGI Everyone character for
a 10-minute agent session and record every state transition. Then replay
the same event log through our Three.js/VRM adapter. If the semantic event
log reproduces equivalent behavior, we have validated renderer-independent
embodiment.

Replace/complement: complements Voqalize-style Performance IR and could
replace a lot of custom browser-avatar/MCP glue. It does not replace
premium Avatar-Forever/Wan/LTX-style photoreal rendering.

